.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Register and parse command line options and read/write configuration files\&. 

A detailed description can be found under \fBOption Parser\fP\&. In addition, we provide the example \fBoptions\&.c\fP\&. 
.SH "Typedef Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "typedef int(* sc_options_callback_t) (\fBsc_options_t\fP *opt, const char *opt_arg, void *data)"

.PP
This callback can be invoked with \fBsc_options_parse\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIopt\fP Valid options data structure\&. This is passed as a matter of principle\&. 
.br
\fIopt_arg\fP The option argument or NULL if there is none\&. This variable is internal\&. Do not store pointer\&. 
.br
\fIdata\fP User-defined data passed to sc_options_add_callback\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Return 0 if successful, -1 to indicate a parse error\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void sc_options_add_bool (\fBsc_options_t\fP * opt, int opt_char, const char * opt_name, int * variable, int init_value, const char * help_string)"

.PP
Add a boolean option\&. It can be initialized to true or false in the C sense\&. Specifying it on the command line without argument sets the option to true\&. The argument 0/f/F/n/N sets it to false (0)\&. The argument 1/t/T/y/Y sets it to true (nonzero)\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIopt\fP A valid options structure\&. 
.br
\fIopt_char\fP Short option character, may be '\\0'\&. 
.br
\fIopt_name\fP Long option name without initial dashes, may be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIvariable\fP Address of the variable to store the option value\&. 
.br
\fIinit_value\fP Initial value to set the option, read as true or false\&. 
.br
\fIhelp_string\fP Help string for usage message, may be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_options_add_callback (\fBsc_options_t\fP * opt, int opt_char, const char * opt_name, int has_arg, \fBsc_options_callback_t\fP fn, void * data, const char * help_string)"

.PP
Add an option that calls a user-defined function when parsed\&. The callback function should be implemented to allow multiple calls\&. The callback may be used to set multiple option variables in bulk that would otherwise require an inconvenient number of individual options\&. This option is not loaded from or saved to files\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIopt\fP A valid options structure\&. 
.br
\fIopt_char\fP Short option character, may be '\\0'\&. 
.br
\fIopt_name\fP Long option name without initial dashes, may be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIhas_arg\fP Specify whether the option needs an option argument\&. This can be 0 for none, 1 for a required argument, and 2 for an optional argument; see getopt_long (3)\&. 
.br
\fIfn\fP Function to call when this option is encountered\&. 
.br
\fIdata\fP User-defined data passed to the callback\&. 
.br
\fIhelp_string\fP Help string for usage message, may be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

